{"id":"word:hebrew:H1058","type":"word","title":"בָּכָה","subtitle":"H1058 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to weep ; generally to bemoan","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בָּכָה (H1058) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 116 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בָּכָה (bâkâh) means to weep ; generally to bemoan First listed occurrence: 1Sam 1 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בָּכָה","transliteration":"bâkâh","pronunciation":"baw-kaw'","strong":"H1058","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1058","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וַ/יֵּ֥בְךְּ","וַ/יִּבְכּֽוּ","וַ/יֵּֽבְךְּ","וַ/יִּבְכּ֑וּ","וַ/יֵּ֑בְךְּ"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3mp",17],["HC/Vqw3ms",17],["HC/Vqw3fs",6],["HC/Vqa",5],["HVqrmsa",5],["HVqrmpa",5],["HR/Vqc",4],["HVqa",4],["HVqi3fs",3],["HVqi3mp",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to weep ; generally to bemoan","usage":"× at all, bewail, complain, make lamentation, × more, mourn, × sore, × with tears, weep.","full":"H1058. bakah בָּכָה 114 verb weep, bewail (Arabic , Aramaic בְּכָא , , Assyrian bakû Zim BP 23, 56 , Ethiopic ) — Qal Perfect ׳בּ Gen 43:14 ; Hosea 12:5 ; וּבָֽכְתָה consecutive Deut 21:13 ; בָּכִ֫יתִּי Job 30:25 , etc.; Imperfect וַיֵּבְךְ Gen 37:35 16 t. ( וַיֵּבְךְּ 27:28 etc.); 3 feminine singular תִּבְכֶּה 1Sam 1:10 2 t.; וַתִּבְכֶּה 1:7 , וַתֵּבְךְּ Gen 21:16 (where ᵐ5 masculine compare Di) + 4 t.; 2 masculine singular תִּבְכֶּה Isa 30:19 ; Ezek 24:16 ; וַתִּבְכֶּה 2Kin 22:19 , וַתֵּבְךְּ 2Sam 12:21 ; 2Chr 34:27 ; 2 feminine singular תִּבְכִּי 1Sam 1:8 ; אֶבְכֶּה Judg 11:37 4 t.; וָאֶבְכֶּה 2Sam 12:22 2 t.; יִבְכּוּ Lev 10:6 3 t.; יִבְכָּי֑וּן Job 31:38 ; Isa 33:7 ; 3 feminine plural תִּבְכֶּינָה Job 27:15 ; Psa 78:64 ; ׳וַתִּב Ruth 1:9 , 14 , etc.; Imperative plural בְּכוּ Jer 22:10 ; Joel 1:5 ; בְּכֶינָה 2Sam 1:24 ; Infinitive absolute בָּכוֺ Isa 30:19 3 t. + Micah 1:10 (where read בְּעַכּוֺ , see עכו ); בָּכֹה 1Sam 1:10 3 t.; construct לִבְכּוֺת Gen 43:30 3 t.; לִבְכֹּתָהּ 23:2 ; Participle בֹּכֶה ( בּוֺכֶה ) Exod 2:6 6 t.; feminine singular בּוֺכִיָּה Lam 1:16 ; plural בֹּכִים ( ׳בּו ) Ezra 3:12 +, etc.; — 1 weep (in grief, humiliation, or joy), absolute Gen 42:24 ; 43:30 (twice in verse); Exod 2:6 ; Num 11:4 , 10 ; 14:1 ; 1Sam 1:7-8 , 10 ; 11:5 ; 30:4 (twice in verse); 2Sam 1:12 ; 3:16 ; 13:36 ; 15:30 (twice in verse); 19:1 ; 19:2 ; 2Kin 8:11-12 , Isa 30:19 (twice in verse); Jer 41:6 ; 50:4 ; Ezek 24:16 , 23 ; Lam 1:2 ; Zech 7:3 ; Joel 1:5 ; 2:17 ; Psa 78:64 ; 126:6 ; compare 69:11 (but on text see Che) Job 27:15 ; Eccl 3:4 (opposed to laugh שׂחק ) Ezra 10:1 ; Neh 8:9 ; Est 8:3 ; once with inanimate subject Job 31:38 יִב ׳תְּלָמֶיהָ its furrows weep ; on Neh 1:4 וָאֶבְכֶּה יָשַׁבְתִּי compare Assyrian attašab abakî , Flood 130ed. Dl Gu § 77 Hpt BAS i. 145 ; of loud weeping וַיִּב ׳הַקּוֺל נָשָׂא Gen 21:16 ; 27:38 ; 29:11 ; Judg 2:4 ; 21:2 ; 1Sam 11:4 ; 24:17 ; 2Sam 3:32 ; 13:36 ; Job 2:12 ; Ruth 1:9 , 14 , compare ׳בּ י ׳בְּאָזְנֵי Num 11:18 , also Job 30:31 . 2 with accusative of congnate meaning with verb בְּכִי Judg 21:2 ; 2Sam 13:36 ; 2Kin 20:3 = Isa 38:3 , compare בִּבְכִי 16:9 , מִבְּכִי Jer 48:32 , & ׳בּ בֶּכֶה חַרְבֶּה Ezra 10:1 ; followed by גָּדוֺל קוֺל 2Sam 15:33 , compare ׳בּ גדול בקול Ezra 3:12 ; weep bitterly יִב ׳מַר Isa 33:7 ; also with infinitive absolute weep intensely, grievously 1Sam 1:10 ; Jer 22:10 ; Lam 1:2 , compare Isa 30:19 & Micah 1:10 (but on text see above) 3 followed by עַל weep upon , i.e. embrace and weep, עַלצֿואריו Gen 45:14 ; 46:29 ; compare 45:15 ; 50:1 ; also ׳בּ עַלמָּֿנָיו 2Kin 13:14 ; see further Gen 33:4 ; 45:14 & אֶתרֵֿעֵהוּ אִישׁ וַיִּבְכּוּ 1Sam 20:41 ; also followed by עַל weep over, for Judg 11:37-38 , 2Sam 3:34 ; Lam 1:16 ; followed by אֶלֹֿ 2Sam 1:24 ; 3:32 ; Ezek 27:31 ; followed by לְ Jer 22:10 ; 48:32 ; Job 30:25 ; followed by מִמְּנִי because of Jer 13:17 ; followed by temporal clause (of occasion of weeping) Gen 50:17 ; Psa 137:1 ; Neh 8:9 . 4 followed by accusative bewail Gen 23:2 ; 37:35 ; 50:3 ; Lev 10:6 ; Num 20:29 ; Deut 21:13 ; 34:8 ; Jeremiah 8:23, compare Isa 16:9 . 5 followed by עַל in sense of burden, annoy with weeping Num 11:13 ; Judg 14:16-17 , compare לִפְנֵי Num 11:20 . 6 ׳בּ י ׳לִפְנֵי of penitent weeping Judg 20:23 (compare Be; see also 21:2 ) Deut 1:45 ; 2Kin 22:19 ; 2Chr 34:27 , compare also Num 25:6 ; joined with fasting Judg 20:26 ; 2Sam 12:21-22 , compare Ezra 10:1 ; so of weeping in anxious entreaty Hosea 4:5 ; on participle as proper name Judg 2:1 , 5 see בֹּכִים below Pi`el Participle feminine singular מְבַכָּה lament Jer 31:25 followed by עַל ; bewail , plural מְבַכּוֺת followed by accusative Ezek 8:14 .","rootNote":"a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 1 7","keyReferences":["1Sam 1 7","1Sam 1 8","1Sam 1 10","1Sam 1 10","1Sam 11 4","1Sam 11 5","1Sam 20 41","1Sam 24 17"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":116,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 1 7","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תִּבְכֶּ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 8","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִבְכִּ֗י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בָכֹ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqa"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִבְכֶּֽה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 11 4","book":"1Sam","chapter":11,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יִּבְכּֽוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 11 5","book":"1Sam","chapter":11,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִבְכּ֑וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3mp"},{"reference":"1Sam 20 41","book":"1Sam","chapter":20,"verse":41,"eng